      "question_index": 3,
      "question_type": "MCQ",
      "question_text": "The real value of ' $\\alpha$ ' for which $\\frac{1-isin\\alpha}{1+2isin\\alpha}$ is purely real is",
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-body\"> <div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>The real value of '  $\\alpha$  ' for which  $\\frac{1-isin\\alpha}{1+2isin\\alpha}$  is purely real is</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div></div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$(n+1)\\frac{\\pi}{2},n \\in N$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->  $(n+1)\\frac{\\pi}{2},n \\in N$ \n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$(2n+1)\\frac{\\pi}{2},n \\in N$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->  $(2n+1)\\frac{\\pi}{2},n \\in N$ \n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$n\\pi,n \\in N$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->  $n\\pi,n \\in N$ \n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$(2n-1)\\frac{\\pi}{2},n \\in N$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->  $(2n-1)\\frac{\\pi}{2},n \\in N$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": null,
      "explanation_text": "Given, $\\frac{1-isin\\alpha}{1+2isin\\alpha}$ is purely real i.e. $\\frac{1-isin\\alpha}{1+2isin\\alpha} \\times \\frac{(1-2isin\\alpha)}{(1-2isin\\alpha)}$ $\\begin{aligned} & =\\frac{1-isin\\alpha-2isin\\alpha+2i^{2}sin^{2}\\alpha}{1-4i^{2}sin^{2}\\alpha} \\\\ & =\\frac{1-3isin\\alpha-2sin^{2}\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha} \\\\ & =\\frac{1-2sin^{2}\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha}+i(\\frac{-3sin\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha}) \\end{aligned}$ which is given to purely real $\\begin{aligned} \\Rightarrow & \\frac{-3sin\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha}=0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & -3sin\\alpha=0 \\Rightarrow sin\\alpha=0 \\end{aligned}$ Hence, $\\alpha=n\\pi,n \\in N$",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>Given,  $\\frac{1-isin\\alpha}{1+2isin\\alpha}$  is purely real</p>\n<p>i.e.  $\\frac{1-isin\\alpha}{1+2isin\\alpha} \\times \\frac{(1-2isin\\alpha)}{(1-2isin\\alpha)}$ </p>\n<p> $\\begin{aligned} &amp; =\\frac{1-isin\\alpha-2isin\\alpha+2i^{2}sin^{2}\\alpha}{1-4i^{2}sin^{2}\\alpha} \\\\ &amp; =\\frac{1-3isin\\alpha-2sin^{2}\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha} \\\\ &amp; =\\frac{1-2sin^{2}\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha}+i(\\frac{-3sin\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha}) \\end{aligned}$ </p>\n<p>which is given to purely real</p>\n<p> $\\begin{aligned} \\Rightarrow &amp; \\frac{-3sin\\alpha}{1+4sin^{2}\\alpha}=0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow &amp; -3sin\\alpha=0 \\Rightarrow sin\\alpha=0 \\end{aligned}$ </p>\n<p>Hence,  $\\alpha=n\\pi,n \\in N$ </p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
      "has_image": false,
