      "question_index": 4,
      "question_type": "MCQ",
      "question_text": "The modulus of the complex number $\\frac{(1+i)^{2}(1+3i)}{(2-6i)(2-2i)}$ is",
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-body\"> <div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>The modulus of the complex number  $\\frac{(1+i)^{2}(1+3i)}{(2-6i)(2-2i)}$  is</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div></div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}$ \n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ \n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}$ \n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": null,
      "explanation_text": "$\\begin{aligned} \\text{Here,} & \\frac{(1+i)^{2}(1+3i)}{(2-6i)(2-2i)} \\\\ = & \\frac{(1+i^{2}+2i)(1+3i)}{4-4i-12i+12i^{2}} \\\\ = & \\frac{2i+6i^{2}}{-8-16i}=\\frac{2i-6}{-8-16i} \\\\ = & \\frac{i-3}{-4-8i} \\\\ = & \\frac{3-i}{(4+8i)} \\times \\frac{(4-8i)}{(4-8i)} \\\\ = & \\frac{12-28i-8}{16+64} \\\\ = & \\frac{4-28i}{80}=\\frac{1-7i}{20} \\\\ = & \\frac{1}{20}-\\frac{7i}{20} \\end{aligned}$ $\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Let}z=x+iy \\\\ & \\because |z|=\\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow |z|=\\sqrt{(\\frac{1}{20})^{2}+(\\frac{7}{20})^{2}} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow |z|=\\frac{1}{20}\\sqrt{50}=\\frac{5}{20}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow |z|=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\end{aligned}$",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p> $\\begin{aligned} \\text{Here,} &amp; \\frac{(1+i)^{2}(1+3i)}{(2-6i)(2-2i)} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{(1+i^{2}+2i)(1+3i)}{4-4i-12i+12i^{2}} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{2i+6i^{2}}{-8-16i}=\\frac{2i-6}{-8-16i} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{i-3}{-4-8i} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{3-i}{(4+8i)} \\times \\frac{(4-8i)}{(4-8i)} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{12-28i-8}{16+64} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{4-28i}{80}=\\frac{1-7i}{20} \\\\ = &amp; \\frac{1}{20}-\\frac{7i}{20} \\end{aligned}$ </p>\n<p> $\\begin{aligned} &amp; \\text{Let}z=x+iy \\\\ &amp; \\because |z|=\\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}} \\\\ &amp; \\Rightarrow |z|=\\sqrt{(\\frac{1}{20})^{2}+(\\frac{7}{20})^{2}} \\\\ &amp; \\Rightarrow |z|=\\frac{1}{20}\\sqrt{50}=\\frac{5}{20}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ &amp; \\Rightarrow |z|=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\end{aligned}$ </p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
      "has_image": false,
      "image_urls": [],
      "topic_tag": "Kcet Complex Numbers - Core Application",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
